  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ALT caporalato TRE: protection, resilience and emergence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to build on the consolidated partnership between the International Organization for Migration (IOM) and the Italian Labour Authority (INL) which, since 2020 and through various projects, have worked together to reduce migrant workers&apos; exposure to labour exploitation and counter trafficking across all economic sectors in Italy. The primary objective is to enhance the efficiency of labour inspections, strengthen national referral mechanisms for victims of labour exploitation and victims of trafficking (VoT), and facilitate the reintegration of victims into the national labour market.The project&apos;s activities include deploying mobile teams of intercultural mediators to support labour inspection activities, providing specialized support in the identification and referral of labour exploitation victims, and raising awareness among vulnerable migrant workers. The project strengthens the capacity of labour inspectors and relevant practitioners through targeted training and enhanced coordination mechanisms to better identify and assist victims of labour exploitation and VoT.This intervention is recognized as a good practice at the European level and by leveraging the synergies between various stakeholders, the project has demonstrated significant success in identifying and referring victims of labour exploitation/VoT.</narrative>
  </description>
